    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0665" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6111/1053: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-01T17:00:00-05:00">November 1, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1175. You are requested to inform the Foreign Office that the appointment of
                    Maxim Litvinov as Soviet Ambassador to Washington is most agreeable to this
                        Government.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d649-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d649-f1" n="24" xml:id="d649-f1-content">
                <p>Under Secretary of State Welles noted on this telegram that it was “approved by
                    the President by telephone Nov. 1, 10:15 a.m.” The contents of the telegram were
                    given to Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs Vyshinsky on November
                    4, 1941.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
